                <pb facs="0222" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.72/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bundy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-17T11:00:00-00:44"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 18—2:19
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>47. Department’s 32, July 15 [<hi rendition="#italic">14</hi>], 6 p.m. Act passed
                    by Legislature granting concession to French Cable Company mentioned Legations
                    cable 24, February 27, 1 p.m. was approved by President. Said act appears in the
                    recently published acts of the Legislature passed at its last session. Copies of
                    these published acts were mailed with Legation’s despatch number 83 dated June
                        23<anchor n="50" xml:id="d107-f1"/> now <hi rendition="#italic">en
                        route.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
